libampdac is a Linux userspace extract of the USB Audio Class 2 isochronous
path from Audiophile Music Player.

Upstream (MIT):
  https://github.com/androidexpert35/Audiophile-Music-Player

The files under native/ are that project's UAC2 engine (descriptor parser,
clock control, ISO pool, DSD/DoP formatters, teardown). This repository does
not include the Android app, JNI, FFmpeg decoder, or UI.

Linux-specific work in this tree (ampdac C ABI, CLI, kernel unbind, Deadbeef
output plugin, udev) is also MIT and lives beside those sources so the library
can be built without the Android Gradle project.

Deadbeef plugin headers under plugins/deadbeef/include/ are from DeaDBeeF
1.10.3 (GPL-2.0) and are used only to compile the optional output plugin.
